<title>GREECE: ATHENS BOURSE PRESIDENT SUES BROKERS FOR FRAUD.</title>
<headline>ATHENS BOURSE PRESIDENT SUES BROKERS FOR FRAUD.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Athens stock exchange president Manolis Xanthakis, on behalf of the bourse, has filed a suit against three officials of Delta Securities for fraud, court sources told Reuters.  </p>
<p>The suit on behalf of the exchange was handed to Athens prosecutor George Koliokostas, who must decide whether to bring charges.</p>
<p>The three Delta Securities officials, Dimitris Argyriadis, Ioanna Gelestathi and Theofanis Gravanis are already facing charges for extensive, repeated fraud after failing to settle with the clearing house and trying to pay with bad cheques.</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
